72ta|n|The son of Helios (Phoebus), that is, the son of light, or of the sun. He is fabled to have obtained permission to drive the chariot of the sun, in doing which his want of skill would have set the world on fire, had he not been struck with a thunderbolt by Jupiter, and hurled headlong into the river Po. ; A genus of oceanic birds including the tropic birds.	n:8uww,94,5~8uww,94,5	N:8uww,87,3~8uww,87,3
72tb|n|A four-wheeled carriage (with or without a top), open, or having no side pieces, in front of the seat. It is drawn by one or two horses. ; See Phaethon. ; A handsome American butterfly (Euphydryas, / Melitaea, Phaeton). The upper side of the wings is black, with orange-red spots and marginal crescents, and several rows of cream-colored spots; -- called also Baltimore.	n:afeu,134,5~afeu,134,5
